# Thresholding — pick a method from the dropdown; its own parameters appear
# below automatically via params().
#
# Adding a new algorithm with Category()=="threshold" makes it show up here
# with its controls, without editing this script at all.
#
# Run this on assets/page.png rather than test.png:
#
#   ./build/Release/tglab.exe scripts/thresholds.tgl assets/page.png
#
# page.png is a synthetic scan -- text under uneven lighting, bright at the top
# left and dim at the bottom right. That gradient is the whole point: a single
# global threshold cannot serve both ends of it, which is what the local methods
# exist to fix. test.png is a smooth gradient with a checkerboard patch, and has
# so little local structure that every local method correctly returns almost
# uniform white on it -- which looks broken but is not.

src = image("page")

op = choose("method", "threshold")

pre   = slider("pre-blur sigma", 0.0, 8.0, 0.0)
blurred = gaussian_blur(src, sigma = pre)

mask = params(op)(blurred)

display(src,     "1 source")
display(blurred, "2 pre-blurred")
display(mask,    "3 mask")
